  I really hope that this topic can be addressed in 3.1 since IMO it
is the single most frustrating feature of the game. I'm referring to
the impossibility of moving past your pet or a friendly monster. I
just died in a game in which I was trapped in a room because I was
blocked in by my pet rats (being a ratwere at the time). It was
extremely frustrating to have to just stand there, unable to back
out. This is also a real nuscience when moving down a long
corridor and getting continuous "You stop to avoid hitting your dog"
messages. It's even worse when one is trying to move through a
room of gremlins. An obvious solution, which I've seen posted before,
is to simply exchange positions of friendly monsters and player
(except shopkeepers presumably). One could then add a 'hit'
command (similar to the 'kick') in case one ever really wanted
to attack a friendly monster. Anyone else have any thoughts on this?



